      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L%C3%A9vis"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city’s modern form began January 1, 2002 when ten municipalities merged, including the original 1861 Lévis.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L%C3%A9vis"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1647 Guillaume Couture became the first French settler in the Lauzon seignory that later became part of Lévis.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L%C3%A9vis"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The historic Davie Shipyard, operating 1829‑1989, is now a National Historic Site museum on Lévis waterfront.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/L%C3%A9vis"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Lévis’s Lowtown hosts railroad yards and wharves, while Hightown atop cliffs is mainly residential.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
